{"id": "wwdc2019-516", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/516", "wordCount": 2499, "segments": [{"start": 15.0, "text": "Hello, everyone."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "My name is Ricky Mondello, and I"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "am so excited to be here to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "today to tell you about What's"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "New in Authentication on Apple"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "platforms, including some very"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "exciting and new APIs in the"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "Authentication Services"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "My goal is to help you get your"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "users signed into your apps as"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "quickly and securely as"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "possible."}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "We're going to talk about five"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "topics today starting with Sign"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "In with Apple."}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "Sign In with Apple is an easy"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "and secure way for users to sign"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "into your apps."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "Signing in is as quick as a few"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "taps and a face ID check."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "Sign In with Apple is a private"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "alternative to other single"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "sign-on providers that you might"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "be aware of."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "And you probably already get the"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "gist of what this capability is"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "about."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "But what I want to do is"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "emphasize a few key points"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "related to how Authentication"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "works already in your apps."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "And the first is that for your"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "users, Sign In with Apple is"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "easier to use than passwords."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "People generally don't love"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "managing passwords."}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "And when users don't have a"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "password, that password can't be"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "a bad password, and it can't get"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "phished, which is good for your"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "users, but it's also good for"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "you."}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "And for you specifically, these"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "accounts are great accounts."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Every single one of the accounts"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "that can be used with Sign In"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "with Apple has strong two-factor"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "authentication that's already"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "used to protect their Apple ID."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "This two-factor authentication"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "involves the user's circle of"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "trusted devices and strong"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "biometrics."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "Having a user start off with"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "this much security is a lot"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "easier than trying to bolt it on"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "after the fact to a"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "password-based account."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "And to help you with fraud,"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "there's information included in"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "the API about how Apple is"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "confident about the account"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "being from a real user, which"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "you're going to really appreciate."}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "And the third point that I want"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "to emphasize about Sign In with"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "Apple is that it is across"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "platform experience, across all"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "of the user's devices."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "If they're signed into their"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "Apple ID, signing into your app"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "is as easy as a quick face ID or"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "touch ID check."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "And thanks to the web and web"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "technologies, Sign In with Apple"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "is available elsewhere."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "And don't worry."}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "We're going to help your users"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "not create a second account for"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "your app if the user already has"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "one that works for them."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "On app launch, your app can"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "check for an existing"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "password-based account saved to"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "the iCloud Keychain even before"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "you show your standard login"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "interface so that users do the"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "right thing."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "If you have a service with user"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "accounts, you and your users can"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "benefit from Sign In with Apple."}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "To learn more about it,"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "including how to adopt it on the"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "web, watchOS, tvOS, the Mac,"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "iPadOS, and iOS, check out"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "Introducing Sign In with Apple"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "in the WWDC app."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "And that's Sign In with Apple, a"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "convenient and private"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "alternative to password-based"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "authentication."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "And password-based"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "authentication is actually my"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "next topic because even in a"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "world with a great, private"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "single sign-on option, passwords"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "are still going to be a part of"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "our lives."}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "And that's why iPhone has"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "Password AutoFill, which makes"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "it quick and easy for users to"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "sign in to your apps on the"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "existing login screens that you"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "already have."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Today, I am very excited to tell"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "you that Password AutoFill is"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "available for iPad apps for Mac"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "with an interface that is"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "specifically tailored to the"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "Mac. Thanks. For users to get this"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "deluxe experience that you see"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "right here, where the exact"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "right credential that the user"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "wants to sign in with is in the"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "list, there's just one thing"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "that you have to do."}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "Once you've brought your app to"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "the Mac, it'll have a new app"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "ID, and that app ID has to be"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "listed on your server in order"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "to tie your app and your website"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "together."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "If you're using webcredentials"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "to do this, your Apple app site"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "association file might look"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "something like this."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "And all you're going to do is"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "add the app ID to this app's"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "array."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "Super easy."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "But if you're using universal"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "links, you'll add the new app ID"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "here as part of the new app ID's"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "key that can take a list."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "This key is new to iOS 13 and"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "macOS Catalina."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "To maintain compatibility with"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "iOS versions before 13, you'll"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "want to keep this apps key with"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "the value of an array and the"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "app ID key that lists your"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "existing iOS app."}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "You really want to do this in"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "order to ensure that universal"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "links keep working for your"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "users who are running iOS 12."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "There are a bunch of new"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "features and universal links"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "this year, including more"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "powerful URL matching."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "And to learn more about those, I"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "encourage you to check out the"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "What's New in Universal Links"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "video in the WWDC app."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Whether on the Mac, iPad, Apple"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "TV, or iPhone, Password AutoFill"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "makes it easy for users to get"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "signed in to apps on your"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "existing login screens."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "But let's take a closer look at"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "this screen right here."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "The user's current task of"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "getting signed into your app?"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "The answer to the problem is"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "It's a small part of the"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "keyboard."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "And this is great, because"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "AutoFill is accommodating the"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "username and password field"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "combination pattern that we've"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "seen for even before when iPhone"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "existed."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "But your app can have an even"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "more streamlined and intentional"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "experience, and with iOS 13,"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "it's easier to do this than ever"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "before."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "The same sign-in experience I"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "showed you earlier in the"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "context of Sign In with Apple,"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "is available to all apps that"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "use passwords."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "And it's available through the"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "authentication services"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "The same API and functionality"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "is also available on macOS"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "Catalina."}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "Let's talk about how to add this"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "functionality to your apps."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "The first step is to write some"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "code using the"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "AuthenticationServices"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "You'll create an"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "AuthorizationController using a"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "password request."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "The AuthorizationController is"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "the same object that you'll use"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "for Sign In with Apple."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "But here we're just using a"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "different kind of request."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "Then you'll set up a delegate as"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "well as an object that will help"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "coordinate presentation of the"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "interface."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "And then it'll tell the"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "controller to perform the"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "request."}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "When the user has selected the"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "account that they want to use,"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "the API will call the delegate,"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "and you can take it from there"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "to complete the sign-in."}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "If didCompleteWithError is"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "immediately called for you, it"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "might mean that your user"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "doesn't have any passwords saved"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "in their iCloud Keychain for"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "your app and website. And then you should just"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "fallback to showing your normal"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "sign-in screen."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "The user can take it from there."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "But if you're sure that you have"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "credentials on a test device and"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "you're seeing the error handler"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "get called, you're going to want"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "to back to checking your"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "associated domains."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "If you've never tied your app"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "and website together before"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "through associated domains,"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "Introducing Password AutoFill"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "for Apps has a step-by-step"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "tutorial that'll take you"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "through it. It's pretty easy."}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "And for universal links, once"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "again, you're going to want to"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "check out the Universal Links"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "video that's in the WWDC app."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "Something about this API that is"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "really awesome is that you can"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "request multiple types of"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "accounts at the same time using"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "the AuthorizationController."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "And this is super handy if you"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "want to check for both a"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "password-based account and Sign"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "In with Apple right around app"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "launch."}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "If you do this, you're going to"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "want to make sure that you"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "handle both types of credentials"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "in the CompleteWithAuthorization"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "delegate method."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "And that's how easy it is to use"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "the new Authentication services"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "APIs to make the process of"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "getting signed into your apps"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "even more streamlined than"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "password AutoFill was able to."}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "As long as we have passwords,"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "there needs to be a healthy way"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "to use them, a safe way to use"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "And that's why iPhone has"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "Automatic Strong Passwords,"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "which encourages users to use a"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "strong, unique password for"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "every single one of their"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "accounts, which greatly improves"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "their security while also being"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "easier to do than making the"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "mistake of trying to create a"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "password by hand."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "But what if one of your users"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "already has a password that's"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "kind of weak?"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Now, in Safari 13 and iOS 13,"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "when a user signs into a website"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "and Safari notices that the"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "password they just used was"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "weak, Safari will prompt the"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "user to go and visit the website"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "to change the password."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "And this is at the moment of"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "sign-in where the user might be"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "thinking about what the account"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "means to them."}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "If the user accepts Safari's"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "offer, they'll be taken over to"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "Settings where they can change"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "their password."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "And with Automatic Strong"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "Passwords, it's just a few taps"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "to get upgraded."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "And, of course, this feature is"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "on the Mac as well with Safari"}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "13."}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "This flow is at its best when"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "your user is taken directly to"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "your website's Change Password"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "page rather than to the homepage"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "of the site."}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "And what's really cool is that"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "this is completely in your"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "control and super easy to"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "implement."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "Websites like Twitter, GitHub,"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "and WordPress.com have already"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "adopted it."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "All you have to do is put a"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "redirect at this path on your"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "server that takes the user to"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "your Change Password webpage,"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "and that's it."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "The redirect can be implemented"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "either as a client-side redirect"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "or a server-side redirect."}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "You can learn more about the"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "well-known URL for changing"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "passwords, which is a proposed"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "standard at this URL."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "You'll also find it pretty"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "easily if you search the web for"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "And that is how iOS 13, iPadOS,"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "and Safari 13 help users upgrade"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "their weak passwords."}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "Some of your apps authenticate"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "using a third-party web service,"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "and if you're doing this, you're"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "probably using a standard like"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "OAuth."}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "The Authentication's Services"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "frameworks"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "ASWebAuthenticationSession is"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "the best way to do this kind of"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "authentication."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "Once a user confirms that"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "they're OK with signing in, the"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "AuthenticationSession will use"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "existing signed-in accounts"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "through Safari's cookies and"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "data in order to let the user"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "sign-in even faster."}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "Sometimes the user will already"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "be signed in to the identity"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "provider, and all they have to"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "do is agree to signing into your"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "And once they do that, they're"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "in. Nice and easy."}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "I am so happy to be able to tell"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "you today that this API is now"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "available on macOS Catalina."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "On macOS Catalina, this API uses"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "the user's preferred web browser"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "for signing in if that web"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "browser supports it."}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "And this is really great,"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "because it means that all of"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "your users will have their"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "browser's password manager or"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "password manager extension"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "available to them in order to"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "help get them signed in."}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "If you're using the"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "AuthenticationSession API, it"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "has a few new features for you"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "to use this year."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "And the first is a more private"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "kind of sign-in."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "Because the"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "AuthenticationSession shares"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "website data with Safari,"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "ASWebAuthenticationSession"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "enables a single sign-on"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "New to iOS 13, your app can"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "choose to deliver a more private"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "experience, an experience that"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "won't leave users logged into"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "the identity provider in their"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "web browser after they've signed"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "into your app."}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "If your app asks for this"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "experience, users won't see this"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "dialog."}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "Instead, they'll be taken"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "directly to the identity"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "provider in order to get signed"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "To do this, set the"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "prefersEphemeral"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "WebBrowserSession property on"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "the session to true before"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "starting the session."}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "By doing this, you give your"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "users more privacy and avoid"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "that confirmation dialog, which"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "overall might be a better"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "experience for your app."}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "Next, supporting multiple"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "windows."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "In iOS 12, the"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "AuthenticationSession API didn't"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "need any information about view"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "or windows from you in order to"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "display its interface."}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "This is because the API was iOS"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "only, and almost all apps drew"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "into a single window."}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "But now with iPadOS and macOS"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "support, you're going to have to"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "help us out a little bit to"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "figure out where to draw the"}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "interface."}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "First, you'll give the session a"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "presentationContextProvider, and"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "that presentationContextProvider"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "will provide a window via the"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "PresentationAnchor method."}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "This is a really easy change and"}, {"start": 939.0, "text": "one that you're definitely going"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "to want to make."}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "One more thing about OAuth."}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "ASWebAuthenticationSession has a"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "deprecated predecessor called"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "SFAuthenticationSession."}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "It's from the Safari Services"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "If you haven't already, you're"}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "going to want to take a moment"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "to switch over."}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "ASWebAuthenticationSession has"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "the new features that we just"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "talked about, and it's available"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "on the Mac."}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "It's, basically, the"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "non-deprecated drop-in"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "replacement for the old API."}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "And that's it for OAuth."}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "This year, macOS supports USB"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "security keys in Safari through"}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "the WebAuthentication standard."}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "I am really happy about this"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "support, especially because I"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "know that a number of you have"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "been asking for it."}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "Depending on who or what you're"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "protecting and the threat models"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "that you're concerned about, you"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "might consider tying user"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "authentication to the physical"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "presence of some kind of"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "hardware device."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "Safari 13 supports USB-based"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "FIDO2-compliant devices with the"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "WebAuthentication standard."}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "It's available as an"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "experimental feature in Seed 1"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "of macOS Catalina, and it'll be"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "on by default in Seed 2."}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "You can also try it out right"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "now if you download Safari"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "Technology Preview."}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "If you're interested in"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "supporting USB security keys,"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "it's really important to offer a"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "great account recovery story,"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "just in case your user's key"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "gets lost, stolen, or broken."}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "And designing account recovery"}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "systems when a hardware token is"}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "involved is really important,"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "but it's not always"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "straightforward."}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "So unless you are already in"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "this business or were seriously"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "considering getting into it,"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "it's more likely that one or"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "more of the other areas that I"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "cover today will be more"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "relevant for your users, your"}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "apps, and your websites."}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "If you develop an app with user"}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "accounts, I have three takeaways"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "from what we've talked about"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "today."}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "First, strongly consider"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "adopting Sign In with Apple."}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "For your users, the best"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "password is no password,"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "especially when it's backed by"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "two-factor authentication and"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "great biometrics."}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "Two, make signing into your app"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "a one-tap experience using the"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "Authentication Services"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "Users don't even need to see a"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "keyboard anymore to get signed"}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "And finally, implement the"}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "well-known URL for changing"}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "passwords."}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "It's really easy to do, takes"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "just a moment, and it makes a"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "huge difference when Safari is"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "going to try to help your users"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "upgrade their passwords."}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "You'll find more information"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "about what I covered today and"}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "more in the WWDC app or on the"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "web."}, {"start": 1138.0, "text": "And that is it for me."}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "Thank you all so much."}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "I really hope you've been having"}]}